<title>SPAIN: DIVING-EUROPEAN CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>DIVING-EUROPEAN CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>SEVILLE 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Diving results from the sixth</p>
<p>day of the European championships on Monday:</p>
<p>Men's 10-metre highboard diving semifinal (Four dives each.</p>
<p>Totals include points carried forward from elimination round on</p>
<p>Sunday. Leading 12 competitors go forward to final starting at</p>
<p>1445 GMT on Monday.)</p>
<p>1. Jan Hempel (Germany) 577.05 points </p>
<p>2. Richard Frece (Austria) 559.98</p>
<p>3. Oleg Janchenko (Ukraine) 550.35</p>
<p>4. Heiko Meyer (Germany) 550.02</p>
<p>5. Vladimir Timoshinin (Russia) 522.33</p>
<p>6. Joroslav Makogin (Ukraine) 521.70</p>
<p>7. Leon Taylor (Britain) 520.47</p>
<p>8. Gilles Emptoz-Lacote (France) 519.96</p>
<p>9. Jimmy Sjodin (Sweden) 515.85</p>
<p>10. Peter Waterfield (Britain) 496.56</p>
<p>11. Alexandr Varlamov (Russia) 458.31 </p>
<p>12. Carlos Guinovart (Spain) 448.02 </p>
<p>13. Claudio Leone (Italy) 446.73 </p>
<p>14. John Johansson (Sweden) 428.55</p>
<p>15. Andrzej Kozdrzanski (Poland) 428.19 </p>
<p>16. Houhannes Autandilyan (Armenia) 411.60 </p>
<p>17. Emil Sabrailov (Azerbaijan) 349.11</p>
